Que: for ascending order "arr[i]>arr[i+1] return true otherwise false" is correct or not?
And:- Galat hoga, agar tumhara intention ye hai ki array sorted hai ya nahi check karna.

Tumhe return true aur return false ka meaning samajhna hoga.
- return true → Array sorted hai.
- return false → Array sorted nahi hai.


Correct logic
Order	                                Condition	            Return          Otherwise return
1. Ascending / Non-decreasing	        arr[i] > arr[i+1]	    false           true
2. Strictly Ascending	                arr[i] >= arr[i+1]	    false           true
3. Descending / Non-increasing	        arr[i] < arr[i+1]	    false           true
4. Strictly Descending	                arr[i] <= arr[i+1]	    false           true


Agar condition invalid nahi hoti, toh loop complete hone ke baad return true karenge.
Example: Ascending
for(int i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {
    if(arr[i] > arr[i+1]) {
        return false;
    }
}
return true;


Agar tum return true condition ke andar likhoge:
if(arr[i] > arr[i+1]) {
    return true;
}
return false;

Toh iska meaning ulta ho jayega: ye check karega ki array mein koi adjacent pair ascending order ko violate kar raha hai ya nahi.

Remember: Invalid condition milne par false, aur poora loop successfully complete hone par true.

Easy trick to remember:
- Ascending → Left element should NOT be greater.
- Descending → Left element should NOT be smaller.
- Strictly → Equal elements are also invalid.

All four approaches have:
- Time Complexity: O(n)
- Auxiliary Space: O(1)

